    333  f1c2							; The two writers share SkPrep (entered by `jmp`, so the call chain stays at
    334  f1c2							; pad 2 + SkLoad 2 + a leaf 2 = 6 stack bytes - the stack mirror is only 8 wide).
    335  f1c2							; SkN = 2 checkpoint, 3 game over. A missing key ends the op, bad data leaves a
    336  f1c2							; zero high score. SkBuf[R_HIGH..] = max(old high, current score) on the way out.
    337  f1c2				   SkCheckpoint
